1. K x K = u u^T + (tau-1) P : True
2. R = P (K x K) / (tau-1) is an involution for EVERY tau (R R = I): True | R - I has rank one, R = I + v u^T/(tau-1) with v = P u = ['-t', '1', '1', '-1']
   R = I + v u^T/(tau-1): True | u.v = -2*(t-1) | v = u only if tau = -1 (then R is the orthogonal reflection I - u u^T/2)
   R x R (16 points): involution: True | trace = 4 => its mirror (the -1 eigenspace) has dimension (16 - trace)/2 = 6 for every tau
3. K * diag(1,-1) * K = 0 -(t-1) ; -(t-1) -(t-1)*(t+1)
3. K * diag(1,-1/tau) * K = (t-1)/t 0 ; 0 -(t-1)
4. K^2 = 2 (t+1) ; (t+1) [1 0 1] | K^3 = [3 1] [2 1 1] ; [2 1 1] [1 2 0 1]
   K^2 has a zero entry iff 1 + tau^2 = 0 (tau = i, -i) or tau = -1 ; K^3 is a multiple of the identity iff tau^2 + tau + 2 = 0
